/* ===================================================== home-first loop construction
   A Big C route needs, in this order:
     1. distance within ±5 % of what was asked
     2. no headwind on the way home (≤2 % of it, allowing roundabouts and turns; more only if nothing else exists)
     3. the straightest possible way home: maximum tailwind angle × distance after the turning point
     4. little strong headwind on the way out (a curved way out instead of straight into the wind)
     5. no road ridden twice, parallel roads included (repeats near the start count less)
     6. paved roads only
     7. ridden roads where possible: popular road-bike roads, fietssnelwegen on the way home
     8. no pointless detours: no dead ends, rivers crossed where the roads cross them
     9. two clearly different options, within 30 s, without overloading the free routing servers
   So the way home is built first and checked on real roads (point 2, 3 and 8 are decided there), and only good ways
   home get a way out, which is shaped to fix the distance (1) and kept clear of the way home (5). */

/* Best stretch (popular road or fietssnelweg) near p that runs along `tangent`; on the way home (homeDir set) it must
